{
  "contract": "halo-phone-nodes",
  "version": 1,
  "about": [
    "Nodes the Android app writes to the user's Realtime Database, captured from the REAL Kotlin writers (SmsSyncEngine.sync() over a fake RTDB; ClipboardEnvelope.node()) in android/halocloud — not hand-typed.",
    "Consumed by BOTH sides: Swift (HaloTests/WireContractTests.swift) decodes every `node` the way the desktop does and must produce `expect`; the Kotlin engine test (H-20b) must reproduce every `node` and decrypt to `expect`.",
    "Ciphertext uses a random nonce per write, so a comparator must NEVER compare `*Enc` values byte for byte: mask every field whose name ends in `Enc`, compare the rest exactly, and compare the decrypted `*Enc` values to `expect`.",
    "Key derivation: PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256(passphrase, base64decode(saltBase64), iterations) -> AES-256-GCM, envelope `v1:` + base64(nonce|ciphertext|tag).",
    "Regenerate only when a wire field intentionally changes, in BOTH Swift and Kotlin in the same change."
  ],
  "crypto": {
    "passphrase": "contract test passphrase 1",
    "saltBase64": "AQIDBAUGBwgJCgsMDQ4PEA==",
    "iterations": 100000
  },
  "uid": "uid-contract",
  "deviceId": "dev-A",
  "paths": {
    "device": "devices/{uid}/{deviceId}",
    "line": "sms/{uid}/{deviceId}/lines/{subscriptionId}",
